      "notes": "# LED indicator\n\nA 5 V input drives a green LED through a 1 kΩ resistor. Copper strips run across columns on the bottom face.\n\nThe cut between columns 9 and 10 in row 2 deliberately isolates TP1. Use the remaining 5V connection guide to route it. The GND wire is insulated, so intermediate crossings do not join copper.\n\nSB1 joins the LED anode strip to the neighboring spare strip. Coordinates use the top view, column then row, counted from 1.",
